    d("self_correct", "Calculate 15% of 240 and add it to 240.", "15% of 240 is 36, so the total is 276.", "Now subtract 10% from that total.", "10% of 276 is 27.6, so the result is 248.4.", "Is that the same as subtracting 10% from 240 and then adding 15%?", "No. 240 minus 10% is 216, and adding 15% of 216 (32.4) gives 248.4. It's the same here because percentage changes multiply: 1.15 x 0.90 = 1.035 either way, and 240 x 1.035 = 248.4. Order doesn't matter when both are percentages of the running total.")
